<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="tempo-and-restarts" data-rev="0">
  <!-- @include-skip files-touched rows and callouts follow the sibling plan fragments' inline markup so the page renders them identically -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">config</span> crates/engine/src/tuning.rs, content/tuning.json</summary><div class="pl-card">A carry window for the carrier (how long and how much a pass costs while he is not pressed), an optional clearances block (the clearance aim spread and the cross clearance values), and the four restart delays at the sourced medians: 13.8, 23.2, 31.8 and 32.5 seconds.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>tuning</td><td>+82 / -8</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/decision.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">A clearance becomes its own kind of kick. An unpressed carrier who has just gained the ball pays a cost on a pass and a clearance for a short window, so he carries or holds. A shot is never charged. Every player still decides every tick.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>decide</td><td>+25 / -6</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/sim.rs, rules/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Only open-play passes count as passes. Clearances and the first kick of each restart are counted under their own keys. Live ticks are counted. A defender can clear a fast pass inside his own penalty area once per flight, and the ball then crosses a line or not as the physics decides.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>play</td><td>+102 / -10</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> observe, snapshot, calibrate report, record schemas</summary><div class="pl-card">Three new match statistics: clearances, restart kicks and seconds of ball in play. The snapshot carries the new counters at the next version. The calibrate report shows ball-in-play minutes per 90 beside the bands. The schema properties are optional.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>records</td><td>+56 / -3</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test-support</span> crates/engine/src/scenario.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">A scripted clearance for tests only.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>seams</td><td>+15</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine/tests/tempo_and_restarts.rs and four updated test files</summary><div class="pl-card">Scenes for a clearance, each restart kick, the throw-in delay, the live-tick count and a cleared cross. Slow tests over 200 matches for passes and accuracy, ball in play and throw-ins, and a census of restart times and corner origins.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>tests</td><td>+400 / -6</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> data-files, protocol and the observability contract</summary><div class="pl-card">The new tuning rows and delays, the pass count described as open-play passes, and the three new statistics keys.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>docs</td><td>+30 / -3</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-danger"><strong>The ball may stay in play for more than 65 minutes (high).</strong> The engine awards fewer stoppages than real matches, so the sourced medians alone may leave about 70 live minutes. Implement stops and reports rather than set a delay above a median.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-danger"><strong>Throw-ins are 20 to 24 per match (high).</strong> The slice expected them in band. The clearance aim and the cross clearance are tuned, and a throw-in always needs a ball over the touchline.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Pass accuracy may leave 75 to 88 percent (medium).</strong> The counting change is measured alone first. The pass weights are secondary levers.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Every seeded result moves (medium).</strong> Each moved expectation is re-derived and recorded.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Goals fall further (low).</strong> The product owner accepted this until the final tuning slice.</aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs">
    <summary>Prior revisions (0)</summary>
    <ul><li>No prior revision.</li></ul>
  </details>
  <style>
    .fragment-plan .pl-files { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files th, .fragment-plan .pl-files td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); vertical-align: top; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files summary { cursor: pointer; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-chip { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid currentColor; margin-right: 6px; opacity: 0.8; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-card { padding: 6px 0 4px 18px; opacity: 0.9; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-risks { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
    @media (max-width: 480px) { .fragment-plan .pl-files th:nth-child(3), .fragment-plan .pl-files td:nth-child(3) { display: none; } }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-plan');
      var files = 16, modules = 7;
      var risks = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.pl-risks .callout').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'plan', artifact: 'plan', counts: { files: files, modules: modules, risks: risks } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
